    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **68 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field following the repository's established pattern for computed owner attributes (a derived getter on the JPA entity + a `readOnly` schema property auto-mapped to the DTO by MapStruct).\n\n**`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `getOwnerSegment()`:\n- TIER = `PREMIUM` when `getMembershipLevel() >= 3`, else `STANDARD`\n- AREA = `METRO` when `getLocality()` is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL` \u2014 reusing the existing `REGION_TIMEZONE` map whose keys are exactly those three regions\n- Returns `\"<TIER>_<AREA>\"`\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` property (string enum, `readOnly`) to the Owner schema so it appears in the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response. MapStruct's `toOwnerDto` maps it automatically by name.\n\nBoth Cp55 cases pass (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known region with email\u2192level 2, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city), and all 68 existing tests remain green.",
